description:
Enable the `style` key, which will be a path to a user's universal style file (`.scss`) like:

```
output: 
  revealjs::revealjs_presentation:
    style: rstudio.scss
```

Processed by the sass package.

This file will need to be added as a sass layer, the complete layers needed when compiled look like:

```
// Default mixins and settings -----------------
@import "template/mixins";
@import "template/settings";
// ---------------------------------------------


// Include theme-specific fonts
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Commissioner:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&display=swap');
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,wght@0,300;1,300;1,600&display=swap');

/*-- scss:defaults --*/
// Override theme settings (see ../template/settings.scss)
// Base settings for all themes that can optionally be
// overridden by the super-theme

// Background of the presentation
$backgroundColor: #f6f5ed;

// Primary/body text
$mainFont: 'Commissioner', sans-serif;
$mainFontSize: 40px;
$mainColor: #333;

// Vertical spacing between blocks of text
$blockMargin: 20px;

// Headings
$headingMargin: 0 0 $blockMargin 0;
$headingFont: 'Fraunces', Impact, sans-serif;
$headingColor: #131888;
$headingLineHeight: 1.2;
$headingLetterSpacing: normal;
$headingTextTransform: uppercase;
$headingTextShadow: none;
$headingFontWeight: normal;
$heading1TextShadow: $headingTextShadow;

$heading1Size: 3.77em;
$heading2Size: 2.11em;
$heading3Size: 1.55em;
$heading4Size: 1.00em;

$codeFont: monospace;

// Links and actions
$linkColor: #DD6164;
$linkColorHover: darken( $linkColor, 20% );

// Text selection
$selectionBackgroundColor: #FF5E99;
$selectionColor: #fff;

// Generates the presentation background, can be overridden
// to return a background image or gradient
@mixin bodyBackground() {
	background: $backgroundColor;
}

/*-- scss:rules --*/
// Base theme template for reveal.js
// Theme template ------------------------------
@import "template/theme";
// ---------------------------------------------

```

where all the imported files were pulled from:
https://github.com/hakimel/reveal.js/tree/master/css/theme/template

revealjs supports different styles of slide numbers. To switch slide numbers on/off and to choose a different slide number style via the same option, slideNumber can contain either a [boolean or a string](https://github.com/hakimel/reveal.js#slide-number).

The translation of the slideNumber from the YAML header in the rmarkdown-file to the Reveal.initialize({})-Block in the HTML-file never surrounds its content with ' ' .  Thus, only true/false is understood by rveal.js. 

At the moment the YAML-header reveal_options-line `slideNumber: true` becomes in the HTML-file:

```
Reveal.initialize({
  // Display the page number of the current slide
  slideNumber: true
});
```

This is great but `slideNumber: 'c/t'` should become `slideNumber: 'c/t'` and not `slideNumber: c/t`

It would be great if during the translation of slideNumber from YAML to Reveal.initialize `'` could be added automagically to everything not `true` or `false`.
